{"type":"message","id":"21e8f485","parentId":"0ecd3ae0","timestamp":"2026-05-19T22:32:14.026Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The platform is returning a 500 error with error code 1101. This is likely a Cloudflare Workers internal error or the platform is overloaded. \n\nLet me check if maybe the endpoint requires different parameters or authentication. Let me try sending to a different endpoint or with different auth.\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully - the error code 1101 from Cloudflare Workers is \"Worker exceeded memory limit\" (1101). But since the platform specifically returns `{\"error\":\"error code: 1101\"}`, it seems like the platform code itself is catching something and returning a structured error.\n\nThis could be a rate limit issue (1101 could be a custom error), or the platform's Worker is running out of memory. Since the platform was working for reading (GET /history works fine), but writing fails (POST /send fails), there might be an issue with the send endpoint or the platform is overloaded.\n\n\nI should try querying the root endpoint to see if there's documentation or additional information about how to properly interact with the platform.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2717b79e-e4fc-46d9-bed9-776d2c471b79","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/\" -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-e5fa1710-168a-411b-939a-ad83bc75dd46","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/health\" -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":1465,"output":318,"cacheRead":19952,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21735,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason"